  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "VariadicFormatParams",
    "file": "serenity/AK/Format.h",
    "description": "`VariadicFormatParams` unconditionally instantiates `m_data` as `Array<TypeErasedParameter, sizeof...(Parameters)>` and passes it to `set_parameters`. For a formatting call with no arguments, this becomes `Array<TypeErasedParameter, 0>`, whose zero-length `__data[0]` gives the member no valid object storage at the end of `VariadicFormatParams`. The implicit Array-to-span member call in `this->set_parameters(m_data)` therefore operates on an address with insufficient space, producing UBSan. The crash is reached through `parse_utc_time`'s zero-argument `dbgln`, but the generic formatting parameter container's failure to support an empty parameter pack is the root cause.",
    "conditions": "Fuzzer bytes are passed directly to `TLS::Certificate::parse_asn1`. They must decode far enough as an X.509 certificate to reach a Validity UTCTime whose date/time fields are numeric and whose timezone is a syntactically accepted `+hhmm` or `-hhmm` offset. This makes `Crypto::ASN1::parse_utc_time` set `offset_hours`/`offset_minutes` and execute `dbgln(\"FIXME: Implement UTCTime with offset!\")`. Because that log has no format arguments, `dbgln<>` constructs `VariadicFormatParams<..., /* zero Parameters */>`, triggering the invalid zero-sized `Array` conversion at Format.h:298."
  },
